                        "glosses": [
                            "An avenue, especially in Ancient Greece."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ddafd40-b2d1-33e9-bc0f-e48d52189fbf",
                        "entry_id": "7f47b46d-29ec-35da-9732-8f75d5d14777",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A walkway to a building, (especially) a ceremonial walkway to a temple or tomb in Ancient Greece or Egypt."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "928b6a24-571c-4958-a93d-19c0fc6a33c2",
                                "sense_id": "6ddafd40-b2d1-33e9-bc0f-e48d52189fbf",
                                "text": "On the 20th [of December, 1828] they remained an hour at Oudi-Essebours or the Valley of Lions, thus named from the Sphinxes which ornament the dromos of a monument constructed under the reign of Sesostris, but a mere provincial edifice, built of stone cemented with mortar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ad79c9b-aca7-4e2e-b3d9-406aba03ff57",
                                "sense_id": "6ddafd40-b2d1-33e9-bc0f-e48d52189fbf",
                                "text": "In Lower Egypt : Busiris (Ruins near el Bahbeyt) ; Heliopolis or On [near Matarieh], only an obelisk still extant ; Tanis (San), a dromos of granite columns ; Sais [Sa el Haggar], considerable ruins, particularly of the Necropolis ; Taposiris [Abusir]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1d796f1-495a-4e8f-82ea-1d940ff61d37",
                                "sense_id": "6ddafd40-b2d1-33e9-bc0f-e48d52189fbf",
                                "text": "The grave chambers are usually quadrangular, with stone walls, roofs formed by projecting stones, and doors which were walled up. There is no dromos."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ee43030-a53a-39bd-81eb-fbb11d5f08bb",
